Walking a chain, and reading the recipe at each hop (#452). `inspect` answers "who made THIS product";
these two verbs answer the chain question ADR-0058 §5 actually poses — what identity did this inherit,
from where, and what recipe made each hop. Tracked inputs: `spec.toml` + `daq.cfg` + `raw.l64` + `vol.bin`.

# === A three-hop chain: the DAQ config, the acquisition it configured, the recon derived from that.
#     Each `derived_from` edge pins its parent's seal, which is what makes the chain walkable. ===

```
$ tessera ingest --spec spec.toml --out out
ingested collection blake3:abdeaaa09e729e2d4d5062d52581d6b56a2befbd620c2ddaeb471d54160909b6 (3 members) -> out
  - blake3:cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c -> blake3_cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c.tsra
  - blake3:ec73a94b678c7606ef782686054b595a9e17e892383ef8d54892eca0d17f1a81 -> blake3_ec73a94b678c7606ef782686054b595a9e17e892383ef8d54892eca0d17f1a81.tsra
  - blake3:db68ac428f07c6868dd21cd8e9e533746926a9e6e8100c8b94a3714648c11def -> blake3_db68ac428f07c6868dd21cd8e9e533746926a9e6e8100c8b94a3714648c11def.tsra

```

# === `generation.config_ref` (ADR-0058 §2) is a digest, not a copy: it points at a config block the
#     product already carries. Plain `inspect` prints the digest and stops there. ===

```
$ tessera inspect out/blake3_cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c.tsra
tessera [..] · product=blob
id            blake3:cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c
name          daq-config
timestamp     2024-01-01T00:00:00Z
producer      ge-listmode-daq/3.2
  git_repo    vig-os/ge-daq
  git_commit  0855f5f
  dirty       false
generation    config_ref blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…
content_hash  blake3:5bc5d3de167d7ec0ee4e87b0ee60e9944a93b48fab00d84c12f5ccb92abf69e6
manifest_hash blake3:6017b90ede78d7921c566ece859366b5f8091ee0866fc9fdcbc24a27615e1a2c
blocks        1
  - data                 Blob blake3:b1ab9e2dd8744279805a000f73ca5a213f306a336cfbcf4ceb43c9338a764046
sources       2
  - ingested_from <- daq.cfg  [blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…]
  - ingested_via_spec <- spec.toml  [blake3:6b12472b3bd2…]

```

# === `--resolve-config` dereferences it, so the recipe reads end to end instead of ending at a hash
#     the operator has to chase by hand. A small text config is printed inline; a large or non-UTF-8
#     one is named with the `tessera extract` command that streams it (nothing is buffered to decide
#     which — the Blob spec records its own size). ===

```
$ tessera inspect --resolve-config out/blake3_cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c.tsra
tessera [..] · product=blob
id            blake3:cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c
name          daq-config
timestamp     2024-01-01T00:00:00Z
producer      ge-listmode-daq/3.2
  git_repo    vig-os/ge-daq
  git_commit  0855f5f
  dirty       false
generation    config_ref blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…
  config      block 'data' (daq.cfg) · 245 B
  media_type  text/plain
  │ # Synthetic DAQ acquisition config — the vendor file a `config_ref` points at.
  │ # Not real acquisition data; every value is illustrative.
  │ detector_ring = LYSO4x9
  │ energy_window_keV = 425-650
  │ coincidence_window_ns = 4.5
  │ tof_cal_ref = cal-2024-01
content_hash  blake3:5bc5d3de167d7ec0ee4e87b0ee60e9944a93b48fab00d84c12f5ccb92abf69e6
manifest_hash blake3:6017b90ede78d7921c566ece859366b5f8091ee0866fc9fdcbc24a27615e1a2c
blocks        1
  - data                 Blob blake3:b1ab9e2dd8744279805a000f73ca5a213f306a336cfbcf4ceb43c9338a764046
sources       2
  - ingested_from <- daq.cfg  [blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…]
  - ingested_via_spec <- spec.toml  [blake3:6b12472b3bd2…]

```

# === `--json` is exactly the sealed manifest, so a resolved config is not part of it. Asking for both
#     is refused rather than silently dropping one flag. ===

```
$ tessera inspect --json --resolve-config out/blake3_cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c.tsra
? 1
error: invalid product: --resolve-config cannot be combined with --json: --json is exactly the sealed manifest, and the resolved config is not part of it. Use one or the other.

```

# === Now the chain. `provenance` walks `derived_from` back to the roots, printing the producer and the
#     recipe for each hop. `[pinned]` means the parent on disk is the exact version the edge committed
#     to. `[external leaf]` is where provenance is SUPPOSED to end — a vendor path or spec file, never a
#     Tessera product — so those are not gaps. ===

```
$ tessera provenance out/blake3_db68ac428f07c6868dd21cd8e9e533746926a9e6e8100c8b94a3714648c11def.tsra
blob · recon-01  [blake3:28d22d3bd83c…]
  ↳ ingested_from vol.bin  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:629eccf35341…
  ↳ derived_from blob · daq-raw  [pinned]
      file      out/blake3_ec73a94b678c7606ef782686054b595a9e17e892383ef8d54892eca0d17f1a81.tsra
      producer  ge-listmode-daq/3.2 (0855f5f)
      recipe    2 config keys
    ↳ ingested_from raw.l64  [external leaf]
        source    blake3:3258a47581e9…
    ↳ derived_from blob · daq-config  [pinned]
        file      out/blake3_cce0dc5eb3dbddfa564a6480bfccdc03f021db403b27381b78a88cce1d11747c.tsra
        producer  ge-listmode-daq/3.2 (0855f5f)
        recipe    config_ref blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…
      ↳ ingested_from daq.cfg  [external leaf]
          source    blake3:b1ab9e2dd874…
      ↳ ingested_via_spec spec.toml  [external leaf]
          source    blake3:6b12472b3bd2…
    ↳ ingested_via_spec spec.toml  [external leaf]
        source    blake3:6b12472b3bd2…
  ↳ ingested_via_spec spec.toml  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:6b12472b3bd2…

8 hop(s) · 6 external leaf/leaves · chain complete

```

# === Hand the recon off on its own (`publish` = a self-contained, history-free artifact) and the chain
#     can no longer be proven FROM THE ARTIFACT ALONE — the parent simply is not there to check
#     against. That is rendered, not raised: exit stays 0, because a chain you cannot resolve from one
#     directory is the normal case, and a verb that failed on it would be useless in a pipeline. ===

```
$ tessera init repo
initialized tessera repository at repo

```

```
$ tessera import repo out/blake3_db68ac428f07c6868dd21cd8e9e533746926a9e6e8100c8b94a3714648c11def.tsra
imported lineage blake3:db68ac428f07c6868dd21cd8e9e533746926a9e6e8100c8b94a3714648c11def
  version blake3:28d22d3bd83cac04982d70eabdadd04f97ad24bd0eced6590d90d97245e73ad1

```

```
$ tessera publish repo blake3:28d22d3bd83cac04982d70eabdadd04f97ad24bd0eced6590d90d97245e73ad1 handover.tsra
published blake3:28d22d3b… → handover.tsra
  history-free, snapshot_of blake3:28d22d3b…

```

```
$ tessera provenance handover.tsra
blob · recon-01  [blake3:56fed17d0571…]
  ↳ ingested_from vol.bin  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:629eccf35341…
  ↳ derived_from blake3:ec73a94b678c7606ef782686054b595a9e17e892383ef8d54892eca0d17f1a81  [unresolved]
      pins      blake3:61297daacb3d… — no product with this lineage was found (try --search / --collection)
  ↳ ingested_via_spec spec.toml  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:6b12472b3bd2…
  ↳ snapshot_of blake3:28d22d3bd83cac04982d70eabdadd04f97ad24bd0eced6590d90d97245e73ad1  [version not present]
      version   blake3:28d22d3bd83c… — not present (publish drops history by design)

4 hop(s) · 2 external leaf/leaves · 1 gap(s) — chain INCOMPLETE

```

# === `--require-complete` is the gate mode: same render, nonzero exit. Use it in CI; leave it off to
#     look at a chain. ===

```
$ tessera provenance --require-complete handover.tsra
? 1
blob · recon-01  [blake3:56fed17d0571…]
  ↳ ingested_from vol.bin  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:629eccf35341…
  ↳ derived_from blake3:ec73a94b678c7606ef782686054b595a9e17e892383ef8d54892eca0d17f1a81  [unresolved]
      pins      blake3:61297daacb3d… — no product with this lineage was found (try --search / --collection)
  ↳ ingested_via_spec spec.toml  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:6b12472b3bd2…
  ↳ snapshot_of blake3:28d22d3bd83cac04982d70eabdadd04f97ad24bd0eced6590d90d97245e73ad1  [version not present]
      version   blake3:28d22d3bd83c… — not present (publish drops history by design)

4 hop(s) · 2 external leaf/leaves · 1 gap(s) — chain INCOMPLETE
error: invalid product: provenance chain for handover.tsra is incomplete (--require-complete): some parents resolved to a different version or were not found. Point --search / --collection at them, or drop --require-complete to see the chain anyway.

```

# === Point it at where the parents live and the gap closes. `snapshot_of` now resolves too: it names a
#     VERSION rather than a lineage, and the walk reports it without descending through it — a
#     published artifact points back at its own lineage, so recursing would look like a cycle. ===

```
$ tessera provenance --search out handover.tsra
blob · recon-01  [blake3:56fed17d0571…]
  ↳ ingested_from vol.bin  [external leaf]
      source    blake3:629eccf35341…
  ↳ derived_from blob · daq-raw  [pinned]
